RFC 001: Server Architecture & Core Loop
1. System Philosophy
Master Engine: Pure Go, deterministic, highly responsive. Uses Mochi-MQTT for event routing and SQLite for persistent state [cite: OurVillage].
Master Clock: The server runs a tick system representing in-game time [cite: OurVillage].
Authority: The server holds absolute state authority [cite: OurVillage].
2. Server Event Loop & Time Management
The server broadcasts tick events on world/global/time every tick interval [cite: OurVillage]:
{
  "tick": 8420,
  "timestamp": "1420-05-12T22:15:00Z",
  "in_game_time": "22:15",
  "is_night": true,
  "weather": "clear"
}


Time-Based Schedule & Curfew Engine
Location Access Control: Mochi-MQTT hooks evaluate requests against server time rules [cite: OurVillage].
Curfew Violations: Unheeded warnings trigger server-forced relocation to streets and logging of violation flags [cite: OurVillage].

